IMPORT prelude

-- Food Safety and Security Act 2025 (Singapore) -- what counts as a food business and which ones need a licence (ss 5, 6, First
-- Schedule, read in part), growing produce for sale (First Schedule Part 2 item 1), food brought in "for private consumption" and
-- reselling it (ss 44, 160, 161), what "unsafe" food is (s 11), supplying unsafe or unsuitable food (ss 146, 147, 150, 151), running
-- unlicensed premises (s 102), disallowed conduct by an unlicensed food business (s 104, fine only), the due diligence and
-- packaged-food defences (ss 164, 166(2)) and the five-year repeat-offender rule.
--
-- Edition: "Informal Consolidation -- version in force from 1/7/2026", as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/FSSA2025.txt;
-- the latest amendment annotated is Act 15 of 2026 wef 01/07/2026 (also Act 9 of 2026 and Act 5 of 2026). s 1: the Act "comes into
-- operation on a date that the Minister appoints by notification in the Gazette". The deposit does NOT say which Parts are in force.
-- Section numbers follow the BODY of the deposit; the arrangement at its head is shifted by one line in places (it lists "Meaning of
-- 'food business'" against 4; the body numbers it 5).
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Chosen for its everyday-life relevance: anyone who sells food, cooks from home for money, grows vegetables for sale
-- or brings food back from a trip meets it. SCOPED: this is a very large Act (over 400 pages). Not encoded: food security and the
-- minimum stockholding requirement (Part 2), licensing of importers and the import/export offences other than s 44 (Part 3),
-- licence grant, conditions and regulatory action, traceability, food workers (s 103), defined food and pre-market approval
-- (Part 5), drinking water (Part 6), directions and recalls (Part 7), handling offences (ss 144, 145, 148, 149), food contact
-- articles, food and health promotion (Part 9), misleading conduct and labelling (Part 10), animal feed and pesticides (Part 11),
-- enforcement, appeals and the transitional Schedule. The First Schedule is read only for the items named below. Regulations
-- made under the Act (which s 104 depends on) were not retrieved.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules conventions. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Food Safety and Security Act 2025 -- food businesses, private imports and unsafe food`

§§ `5, 6 and First Schedule -- food business and licensable food business`

-- s 5(1): "food business" means a business, undertaking or activity that involves production of primary produce, handling of food
-- intended for supply, or the supply of food, "regardless of whether ... of a commercial, charitable or community nature or whether
-- it involves the handling or the supply of food on one occasion only". (2): it "includes a food business carried on as a home
-- business". (3): it does NOT include (a) an intermediary providing, for reward, premises or services "(such as an internet service
-- provider or an online auction location)"; (b) one that provides services for trading in food "(such as an event organiser or an
-- organiser of a market at which food is sold)".
-- s 6(1): a "licensable food business" is a food business in Singapore within a class in the First Schedule.
-- First Schedule Part 1 (retail): item 1 eating places "in premises (but not a home)"; item 4 takeaway or ready-to-eat food from
-- "premises (but not a home)"; item 5 selling food in a public place from temporary premises or a vehicle; item 8 a catering
-- service where food is "prepared and served to consumers of the food away from the food premises" for a predetermined type,
-- number, time and cost -- with NO home exclusion; item 11 a food stall in a temporary fair. Part 2 (non-retail): item 4
-- manufacturing, kneading, mixing, forming etc. "for the purpose of sale to any other food business" -- also with NO home
-- exclusion.
-- The licensable column below is a reading of those items alone, on the stated facts.
DECLARE Activity IS ONE OF
    `a restaurant with seating`
    `a bubble tea kiosk`
    `a home baker selling cakes to the public`
    `a one-off charity bake sale from a home`
    `a home cook catering a party at the client's venue`
    `a home baker supplying cakes to a cafe for resale`
    `an online food delivery platform`
    `a night market organiser`
    `a food stall at a temporary fair`

GIVEN `the activity` IS AN Activity
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the activity is a food business` IF
    CONSIDER `the activity`
    WHEN `an online food delivery platform` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a night market organiser` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `the activity` IS AN Activity
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the activity falls within a First Schedule class read here` IF
    CONSIDER `the activity`
    WHEN `a restaurant with seating` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a bubble tea kiosk` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a home cook catering a party at the client's venue` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a home baker supplying cakes to a cafe for resale` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a food stall at a temporary fair` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the activity` IS AN Activity
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the activity needs a food business licence` IF
    `the activity is a food business` `the activity` AND `the activity falls within a First Schedule class read here` `the activity`

§§ `First Schedule Part 2 item 1 -- growing fruit and vegetables`

-- Part 2 item 1: licensable is "any primary production activity other than -- (a) the cultivation of -- (i) any plant which is not
-- for sale; ... (iii) not more than 200 kilograms in a single month of fruits or vegetables, or both, by a method that does not
-- involve the use of -- (A) any excreta (human or animal); or (B) any plant pesticide to which Division 3 of Part 11 applies".
GIVEN `grown for sale` IS A BOOLEAN, `kilograms grown in the month` IS A NUMBER, `uses excreta` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `uses a regulated plant pesticide` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `growing the produce needs a licence` IF
        `grown for sale`
    AND (   `kilograms grown in the month` GREATER THAN 200
         OR `uses excreta`
         OR `uses a regulated plant pesticide`)

§§ `44 -- food imported for private consumption`

-- s 44(1): food is taken to be imported for private consumption if (a) not "as a trade sample or for use in any food business";
-- (b) not "for the purpose of donating it to other persons in Singapore"; (c)(i) "a total weight of not more than 15 kilograms
-- (inclusive of any eggs)" and (ii) eggs, "a clutch of not more than 30 eggs" (or other prescribed figures); and (d) "imported by a
-- single person who is an individual". (3): "subsection (1) does not extend to any food of higher regulatory concern". (4) lists
-- meat other than pork, beef, lamb, mutton, venison, chicken, duck, turkey, goose, quail or domesticated pigeon; puffer fish;
-- fertilised eggs; blood products "such as blood curd"; raw or unpasteurised liquid milk; ANY chewing gum; defined food.
DECLARE Food IS ONE OF
    `pork floss`
    `chicken`
    `hen's eggs`
    `snacks and sweets`
    `crocodile meat`
    `puffer fish`
    `blood curd`
    `unpasteurised milk`
    `chewing gum`

GIVEN `the food` IS A Food
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the food is of higher regulatory concern` IF
    CONSIDER `the food`
    WHEN `crocodile meat` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `puffer fish` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `blood curd` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `unpasteurised milk` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `chewing gum` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the food` IS A Food, `brought in by one individual` IS A BOOLEAN, `for a food business or as a trade sample` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `to donate in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN, `total kilograms` IS A NUMBER, `number of eggs` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the food counts as imported for private consumption` IF
        `brought in by one individual`
    AND (NOT `for a food business or as a trade sample`)
    AND (NOT `to donate in Singapore`)
    AND `total kilograms` AT MOST 15
    AND `number of eggs` AT MOST 30
    AND (NOT `the food is of higher regulatory concern` `the food`)

§§ `160, 161 -- supplying food imported for private consumption`

-- s 161(1): a person is guilty if (a) the person supplies any food; (b) the food is none of "(i) a prohibited food; (ii) a food of
-- higher regulatory concern mentioned in section 44(4)"; (c) it was imported; and (d) "imported on the basis that it was for private
-- consumption only". (2): strict liability. (3): individual $5,000 or 3 months; otherwise $10,000. s 160 is the same offence with
-- knowledge: individual $15,000 or 6 months ($30,000 or 12 months repeat); otherwise $30,000 ($60,000).
-- Food of higher regulatory concern is carved out of this offence, presumably because it cannot be brought in as private
-- consumption in the first place (s 44(3)) -- that reason is an inference; the Act does not state it.
GIVEN `supplies the food` IS A BOOLEAN, `the food` IS A Food, `is a prohibited food` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `imported on a private-consumption basis` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `supplying it is a strict liability offence under section 161` IF
        `supplies the food`
    AND (NOT `is a prohibited food`)
    AND (NOT `the food is of higher regulatory concern` `the food`)
    AND `imported on a private-consumption basis`

§§ `11 -- unsafe food`

-- s 11(1): food is unsafe "if it would be likely to cause physical harm to an individual who might later consume it", assuming it is
-- properly processed and consumed according to its reasonable intended use. (2): NOT unsafe merely because (a) of personal
-- preference; (b) objection "on moral, ethical, cultural, spiritual or religious grounds"; (c) "its consumption in inappropriate
-- quantities may damage an individual's health"; or (d) it "is unhealthy for any individual who has an allergy or other personal
-- health condition".
DECLARE Concern IS ONE OF
    `likely to cause physical harm when eaten as intended`
    `a customer is allergic to it`
    `a religious objection`
    `harmful only if eaten in excess`
    `a customer dislikes it`

GIVEN `the concern` IS A Concern
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the concern makes the food unsafe` IF
    CONSIDER `the concern`
    WHEN `likely to cause physical harm when eaten as intended` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `146, 147, 150, 151, 102, 104, 161 -- maximum fines`

-- s 146 (supplying food one knows or ought to know is unsafe): individual $25,000 or 12 months, repeat $50,000 or 24 months;
-- otherwise $50,000, repeat $100,000. s 147 (strict liability): individual $10,000 or 6 months; otherwise $20,000; no repeat tier.
-- s 150 (unsuitable, knowing): $15,000 / $30,000 repeat; otherwise $30,000 / $60,000. s 151 (strict): individual $8,000 or 3 months;
-- otherwise $15,000. s 102 (unlicensed premises): $15,000 / $30,000; otherwise $30,000 / $60,000. s 104: "a fine not exceeding
-- $5,000". s 161: $5,000; otherwise $10,000.
-- "Repeat offender": convicted on "at least one other earlier occasion within the period of 5 years immediately before" the current
-- conviction (earlier offences under the repealed Sale of Food Act 1973 and other Acts count for some sections; not modelled).
DECLARE Offence IS ONE OF
    `supplying unsafe food knowingly`
    `supplying unsafe food strict liability`
    `supplying unsuitable food knowingly`
    `supplying unsuitable food strict liability`
    `unlicensed licensable food business`
    `disallowed conduct by an unlicensed food business`
    `reselling private-import food strict liability`

GIVEN `convicted of the same offence before` IS A BOOLEAN, `years since the earlier conviction` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is a repeat offender` IF
    `convicted of the same offence before` AND `years since the earlier conviction` AT MOST 5

GIVEN `base` IS A NUMBER, `repeat` IS A NUMBER, `is a repeat offender` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the tier` MEANS IF `is a repeat offender` THEN `repeat` ELSE `base`

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence, `is an individual` IS A BOOLEAN, `is a repeat offender` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine` MEANS
    IF `is an individual`
    THEN CONSIDER `the offence`
         WHEN `supplying unsafe food knowingly` THEN `the tier` 25000 50000 `is a repeat offender`
         WHEN `supplying unsafe food strict liability` THEN 10000
         WHEN `supplying unsuitable food knowingly` THEN `the tier` 15000 30000 `is a repeat offender`
         WHEN `supplying unsuitable food strict liability` THEN 8000
         WHEN `unlicensed licensable food business` THEN `the tier` 15000 30000 `is a repeat offender`
         WHEN `disallowed conduct by an unlicensed food business` THEN 5000
         WHEN `reselling private-import food strict liability` THEN 5000
    ELSE CONSIDER `the offence`
         WHEN `supplying unsafe food knowingly` THEN `the tier` 50000 100000 `is a repeat offender`
         WHEN `supplying unsafe food strict liability` THEN 20000
         WHEN `supplying unsuitable food knowingly` THEN `the tier` 30000 60000 `is a repeat offender`
         WHEN `supplying unsuitable food strict liability` THEN 15000
         WHEN `unlicensed licensable food business` THEN `the tier` 30000 60000 `is a repeat offender`
         WHEN `disallowed conduct by an unlicensed food business` THEN 5000
         WHEN `reselling private-import food strict liability` THEN 10000

§§ `102 -- unlicensed premises`

-- s 102(1): an owner or occupier who "uses, or allows the premises to be used, to carry on a licensable food business" commits an
-- offence unless a current licence holder or exempt under s 320 or 321. (5): not guilty if the person proves, on a balance of
-- probabilities, that the person "had no knowledge and could not with reasonable diligence have ascertained" the use AND "as soon
-- as practicable after becoming aware ... took all reasonable steps to stop that use".
GIVEN `is an owner or occupier` IS A BOOLEAN, `premises used for a licensable food business` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `holds a current licence or is exempt` IS A BOOLEAN, `could not have known` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `took all reasonable steps to stop it once aware` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the owner or occupier is guilty under section 102` IF
        `is an owner or occupier`
    AND `premises used for a licensable food business`
    AND (NOT `holds a current licence or is exempt`)
    AND (NOT (`could not have known` AND `took all reasonable steps to stop it once aware`))

§§ `164, 166(2) -- defences`

-- s 164(1): a defence to a Part 8 offence to prove that the offence was due to "an act or omission of another person" or "an accident
-- or some other cause outside the control of the person charged", and that the person "took all reasonable precautions and
-- exercised all due diligence". (2): "another person" does not include an employee or agent (or, for an entity, an officer).
-- (3): "this defence does not apply if the person charged imported the food".
GIVEN `caused by another person or an outside cause` IS A BOOLEAN, `that other person was the accused's employee or agent` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `took all reasonable precautions and due diligence` IS A BOOLEAN, `the accused imported the food` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the due diligence defence is available` IF
        `caused by another person or an outside cause`
    AND (NOT `that other person was the accused's employee or agent`)
    AND `took all reasonable precautions and due diligence`
    AND (NOT `the accused imported the food`)

-- s 166(2): to a charge under s 146, 147, 150 or 151, a defence to prove that the person "bought the food in a package and supplied it
-- in the same package and in the same condition" AND "could not reasonably have found out that supplying the food would constitute
-- the offence".
GIVEN `bought and supplied in the same package and condition` IS A BOOLEAN, `could not reasonably have found out` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the packaged food defence is available` IF
    `bought and supplied in the same package and condition` AND `could not reasonably have found out`
